{{also|ljuga|leogan}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ljúga||to lie|lang=non}}.

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|laug|laugum|logið}}

# {{context|intransitive}} to [[lie]], to tell [[lies]]
#: ''Hún '''lýgur''' alltaf að mér.''
#:: She's always '''lying''' to me.
#: ''Ertu að '''ljúga'''?''
#:: Are you '''lying'''?
#: ''Að '''ljúga''' til nafns.''
#:: To '''lie''' about one's name.
#: ''Hún '''laug''' því að honum að hún væri ógift.''
#:: She '''lied''' to him about being unmarried.
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[lie]] to someone, to tell [[lies]] to someone
#: ''Stjórnmálamenn hafa [[ljúga fullan|'''logið''' þig fullan]]!''
#:: Politicians have filled you with '''lies'''!
# {{context|transitive|governs the dative}} to [[lie]] about something, to tell [[lies]] about something
#: ''Ég er á þrettán bíla. — Þú '''lýgur''' því!''
#:: I own thirteen cars. — That's a '''lie'''!
#: ''Hann '''laug''' þessu!''
#:: He '''lied''' about this!
#: ''Hann lýgur því að hann eigi bíl.''
#:: He's '''lying''' about having a car.

